From 95f65754daa4f9c141ff390a2c35f69f46506baf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:32:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bootwait: back to the side-by-side lockup, left edge aligned
 with the subtitle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reverts the stacked lockup to bootscreen7's layout (ring + "PICO Z /
LOADER" side by side, subtitle "Pico Z Loader ・ Raspberry Pi Pico W /
x68kzremotedrv", rows as before) and only moves the logo row: its left
edge is the subtitle's left edge, so the ring sits above "Pico Z
Loader". Keeps the band/plane blit storage. waiter_test.py checks the
alignment instead of the centring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
